@startuml fdr0006-card-lifecycle
' Runtime lifecycle of one holder card (FDR 0006, "The holder: fibby as a
' virtual PIV card" and "The holder service"): mint, use, refusal, approval,
' teardown. Companion to docs/features/0006-fibby-guarded-key-holder.md.
'
' Regenerate the rendered image with:  just codemod-diagrams
' The .puml is the source of truth; the .svg render is local-only and gitignored.

title Holder card lifecycle — one virtual card per principal (FDR 0006, phases (c) to (e))

skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultTextAlignment center
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDF0
  BorderColor #B8A100
}

participant "session\n(agent scope,\nbound)" as S
participant "sibling session\n(agent scope,\nnot bound)" as X
participant "approver\n(frontend scope)" as A
participant "holder agent\n(service account)" as H
participant "fibby\n(own account,\nguarded memory)" as F

== Mint (phase d) ==
S -> H : mint@piggy
H -> H : read peer creds + cgroup\nrefuse if scope maps to neither
alt live cards < cap
  H -> F : control socket: create card\n(ed25519, PIN never, touch policy)
  F -> F : generate key + self-signed cert\nin guarded memory
  F --> H : card id
  H -> H : record binding\ncard <-> principal <-> scope
  H --> S : public key
else cap reached
  H --> S : refused: card cap
  note right of S
    FDR 0032: session start is
    refused; no tier-1 fallback
  end note
end

== Use ==
S -> H : sign (key, data)
H -> H : binding matches caller scope
H -> F : PC/SC: select slot, sign
alt touch policy on key
  F --> H : touch needed
  H -> A : approve? (key, principal, scope)
  note right of H
    only a frontend-scope peer
    may answer; an agent-scope
    process cannot approve itself
  end note
  alt approved
    A --> H : approve
    H -> F : continue
  else denied or timed out
    A --> H : deny
    H --> S : refused: not approved
  end
end
F --> H : signature
H --> S : sshsig

X -> H : sign (same key, data)
H -> H : no binding for this scope
H --> X : refused

== Teardown (whichever comes first) ==
alt owner retires
  S -> H : retire@piggy (key)
else bound cgroup disappears
  H -> H : observes scope exit
end
H -> F : control socket: destroy card
F -> F : wipe key material\nthen remove card
F --> H : done
H -> H : drop binding

note over F
  No private key crosses any socket, in either direction.
  A holder restart wipes every card; sessions mint again.
end note
@enduml
